{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"16907fe07c4bb266d28d66d5996b9f9dfe9a0d925dbb68ba0e09c89b36b5cb0d","digest":{"component_or_area":"test infrastructure / conftest fixture","key_entities":["_rebar_repo_template","tests/interfaces/conftest.py","rebar.list_tickets()","test_template_stays_virgin","tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py","REBAR_ROOT",".rebar","MonkeyPatch.context()"],"problem_keywords":["fixture assertion","test isolation","template invariant","ticket seeding","virgin state"],"propositions":["The _rebar_repo_template fixture asserts .rebar absence but does not assert the template contains no tickets, violating the acceptance criterion from ticket 699f.","When a test-level assertion in test_template_stays_virgin is the only no-tickets check, narrowed pytest runs like 'pytest tests/interfaces/store' lack protection against pre-seeded templates.","The missing assertion must execute inside the MonkeyPatch context where REBAR_ROOT and cwd are pinned, because it calls rebar.list_tickets() which requires that environment.","Adding rebar.list_tickets() == [] inside the MonkeyPatch context, before the context exits, enforces the invariant at fixture construction time and protects all consumers regardless of test selection."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787710632240510001,"uuid":"abe8ceb6-3bcc-4664-afb7-d8a925bd8b3a"}